{"name":"Owl Manner Malt","hex":"#c0af87","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"owl","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Old Welsh."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various birds of prey of the order Strigiformes, families Strigidae and Tytonidae, that are primarily nocturnal and have forward-looking, binocular vision, limited eye movement, and good hearing. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A person seen as having owl-like characteristics, especially appearing wise or serious, or being nocturnally active."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/owl"},{"term":"manner","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Mode of action; way of performing or doing anything.","Characteristic mode of acting or behaving; bearing."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To instill manners into."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manner"},{"term":"malt","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Malted grain (sprouted grain) (usually barley), used in brewing and otherwise.","Malt liquor, especially malt whisky."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To convert a cereal grain into malt by causing it to sprout (by soaking in water) and then halting germination (by drying with hot air) in order to develop enzymes that can break down starches and proteins in the grain.","To become malt."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/malt"}],"entries":[{"title":"Owl","blocks":[{"text":"Owls are birds from the order Strigiformes, which includes over 200 species of mostly solitary and nocturnal birds of prey typified by an upright stance, a large, broad head, binocular vision, binaural hearing, sharp talons, and feathers adapted for silent flight. Exceptions include the diurnal northern hawk-owl and the gregarious burrowing owl."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Bubo_bubo_sibiricus_-_01.JPG/330px-Bubo_bubo_sibiricus_-_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Owl","wikidata":"Q25222"},{"title":"Malt","blocks":[{"text":"Malt is any cereal grain that has been made to germinate by soaking in water and then stopped from germinating further by drying with hot air, a process known as \"malting\".\nMalted grain is used to make beer, whisky, malted milk, malt vinegar, malt syrup, confections, flavored drinks, and some baked goods. Malted grain that has been ground into a coarse meal is known as \"sweet meal\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Gr%C3%BCnmalz.jpg/330px-Gr%C3%BCnmalz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malt","wikidata":"Q152024"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Owl_range.png/500px-Owl_range.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Owl_range.png/1280px-Owl_range.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Owl_range.png/500px-Owl_range.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOwl_range.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Chouettes.jpg/500px-Chouettes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Chouettes.jpg/1280px-Chouettes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Chouettes.jpg/500px-Chouettes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tawny owl (Strix aluco), left, and western barn owl (Tyto alba), right, belonging respectively to the Strigidae 